From 53f54bed278908721e282bbf581691571ed57b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 05:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add experimental Vivado XSim flow for tb_pulp

The repository only ships a QuestaSim/ModelSim flow (sim/Makefile,
sim/tcl_files) plus an abandoned Incisive one. These scripts drive
xvlog/xvhdl/xsc/xelab/xsim from the same bender-generated source list.

- gen_filelists.sh: emits xsim/sv.f and xsim/vhdl.f from
  `bender script flist -t rtl -t test`, splitting VHDL out for xvhdl and
  dropping the DPI-only sources (dpi_models.sv, tb_driver.sv, SimDTM.sv)
  that are never instantiated when ENABLE_DPI/ENABLE_EXTERNAL_DRIVER and
  TARGET_RT_DPI are 0.
- fix_bender_typos.sh: works around two upstream manifests that name
  files which do not exist - common_cells v1.24.0 lists
  src/deprecated/clk_div.s (the file is clk_div.sv) and adv_dbg_if lists
  rtl/adbg_axi_biu.sv, with a trailing comma. bender >= 0.29.0 rejects
  these with [E31]; 0.25.2, which the Makefile pins, does not.
- dpi_stub.c: supplies jtag_tick so xelab resolves SimJTAG, which
  tb_pulp instantiates unconditionally but leaves disabled when
  ENABLE_OPENOCD is 0.

Not expected to elaborate as-is on Vivado 2019.1: pulp_soc and
pulp_cluster rely heavily on arrays of SystemVerilog interfaces.

